WEBVTT

00:03.200 --> 00:06.100
All this rain lately sure is a bother.

00:06.100 --> 00:08.080
At least it's regular rain.

00:08.080 --> 00:11.240
It's been raining nothing but 
mackerel at my place lately.

00:11.600 --> 00:14.790
Grilled, simmered, I'm sick of it all.

00:14.790 --> 00:18.740
Well, fatty fish you either love or hate...

00:25.180 --> 00:26.350
A train?

00:26.890 --> 00:28.770
Don't be stupid.

00:28.770 --> 00:32.360
The only thing still running is the Ikebus.

00:43.400 --> 00:44.800
Too fast, too fast, too fast!

00:44.800 --> 00:46.280
Shizuru-chan, calm down!

00:46.280 --> 00:49.750
Go, go, go!

00:51.280 --> 00:52.510
Hold it!

00:52.510 --> 00:55.030
Ikebukuro Station has bay platforms!

00:55.030 --> 00:57.560
Huh? What's a bay platform?!

01:04.860 --> 01:06.650
Is this Ikebukuro?!

01:06.920 --> 01:08.780
I thought we were goners.

01:08.780 --> 01:09.670
Are you okay?

01:09.670 --> 01:10.990
No one hurt?

01:10.990 --> 01:12.130
We did it, though!

01:12.130 --> 01:14.490
We've finally arrived in Ikebukuro!

01:14.490 --> 01:19.280
You see, a bay platform is when 
it's a dead end, like this...

01:20.430 --> 01:21.880
What's up, Pochi-san?

01:23.560 --> 01:24.900
We have intruders!

01:24.900 --> 01:25.790
Eliminate them!

01:25.790 --> 01:27.370
What's this, now?

01:27.370 --> 01:28.900
Attack force, advance!

01:28.900 --> 01:30.810
No questions asked, huh?!

01:35.150 --> 01:36.930
Yoka-chan's scent?

01:36.930 --> 01:37.780
Let's go!

01:37.780 --> 01:38.730
Yeah!

01:38.730 --> 01:40.130
Wait up!

01:56.300 --> 02:00.050
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

03:12.750 --> 03:14.550
Are you awake?

03:14.550 --> 03:16.950
Breakfast is ready.

03:20.550 --> 03:22.690
Ah, yeah.

03:24.340 --> 03:26.640
What's for breakfast today?

03:26.910 --> 03:31.590
Dried horse mackerel, mushroom scrambled eggs,
and bitter melon miso soup.

03:31.900 --> 03:33.360
Sounds good.

03:32.140 --> 03:37.650
Episode 11       Maybe She's a Lost Cause...

03:33.890 --> 03:36.680
You served bitter melon before, I think...

03:36.680 --> 03:38.470
Do you like bitter melon?

03:38.470 --> 03:41.270
No, I wouldn't say that.

03:41.270 --> 03:43.020
Do you not like bitter melon, Yoka-sama?

03:43.440 --> 03:45.240
If so, in the future...

03:44.500 --> 03:46.390
I'm fine with it.

03:46.390 --> 03:48.880
It just gives me a strange feeling.

03:49.590 --> 03:51.120
Strange in what way?

03:51.410 --> 03:53.630
I'm not so sure myself.

03:53.630 --> 03:57.580
It's not like I've eaten it that often, 
but it feels nostalgic in a way.

03:57.580 --> 03:59.130
That's why I said it's strange.

03:59.130 --> 04:00.040
I see.

04:00.800 --> 04:03.820
Where'd you say this was from?

04:04.360 --> 04:05.220
Well...

04:08.060 --> 04:09.020
What?

04:13.950 --> 04:14.840
Found someone.

04:14.840 --> 04:16.690
Let's ask him!

04:17.050 --> 04:18.200
Excuse me.

04:18.200 --> 04:19.690
Could we have a moment of your time?

04:20.950 --> 04:23.530
We're looking for someone 
named Nakatomi Yoka.

04:26.020 --> 04:27.880
Whoa, he's huge.

04:27.880 --> 04:28.830
A kitchen smock?

04:28.830 --> 04:30.100
Behave, now.

04:33.210 --> 04:34.660
Huh? What is it?

04:36.050 --> 04:37.160
What's wrong?

04:37.160 --> 04:39.600
Is it that Kontaro again?

04:45.250 --> 04:45.850
Yo...

05:07.700 --> 05:09.110
How cute.

05:09.650 --> 05:11.480
Is this your dog?

05:11.480 --> 05:13.460
I had a dog a long time ago.

05:13.460 --> 05:14.920
His name was Pochi-san.

05:14.920 --> 05:17.200
What's your name?

05:18.800 --> 05:20.860
Hey, this <i>is</i> Pochi-san!

05:20.860 --> 05:22.400
How can you not tell?!

05:22.400 --> 05:25.930
We came from Agano to find you, Yoka-chan.

05:25.930 --> 05:27.550
You're Yoka-chan, aren't you?

05:39.040 --> 05:41.320
Who <i>are</i> you people?

05:42.100 --> 05:44.440
Could it be you're still mad?

05:47.220 --> 05:48.450
About what?

05:48.720 --> 05:51.210
Why would I be mad?

05:51.210 --> 05:52.290
Well...

06:08.090 --> 06:11.770
I suddenly feel... really terrible...

06:12.310 --> 06:15.160
Like something's stabbing my chest...

06:15.160 --> 06:16.400
Wait, Yoka-chan.

06:16.400 --> 06:18.400
Do you not recognize us?

06:18.400 --> 06:20.220
No way! Amnesia?

06:20.220 --> 06:23.540
Did she get wibble-wobble surgery, 
like Zenjiro-san?

06:23.540 --> 06:24.570
Oh, no!

06:28.610 --> 06:30.620
My name is Nakatomi Yoka.

06:31.120 --> 06:33.330
I'm in high school, and I love astronomy.

06:33.750 --> 06:36.620
I study diligently every day 
here in Ikebukuro.

06:36.950 --> 06:38.440
Studying is fun.

06:38.440 --> 06:40.790
I like learning about new things.

06:40.790 --> 06:42.570
It broadens my perspective.

06:42.570 --> 06:44.620
And my dream when I grow up...

06:46.250 --> 06:49.090
My dream... when I grow up...

06:49.720 --> 06:50.340
Yok—

06:53.210 --> 06:54.350
Shizuru-chan!

06:55.510 --> 06:56.940
Yoka-chan?

07:00.490 --> 07:01.720
Yoka-sama.

07:01.720 --> 07:03.100
Please control yourself.

07:03.100 --> 07:05.150
My name is Nakatomi Yoka...

07:05.150 --> 07:06.300
Listen to me, Yoka!

07:06.300 --> 07:07.140
You see—

07:08.750 --> 07:09.480
Found them.

07:11.170 --> 07:13.550
I didn't think you'd find her so soon.

07:13.550 --> 07:16.410
Annoying vermin, out to harm the princess!

07:16.410 --> 07:18.570
Such impudence, before our 
very own Yoka-hime!

07:18.570 --> 07:20.790
You're a real pack of scoundrels!

07:20.790 --> 07:22.130
That is to say, enemies!

07:22.130 --> 07:23.050
Take them down!

07:23.050 --> 07:25.440
In other words, pulverize them!

07:25.440 --> 07:26.840
Hey, they mean business!

07:26.840 --> 07:28.080
We'll die!

07:28.080 --> 07:28.930
Yoka!

07:28.930 --> 07:30.460
Wait, Yoka!

07:30.460 --> 07:31.980
Shizuru-chan, not now!

07:31.980 --> 07:32.910
Everyone, this way!

07:32.910 --> 07:34.990
We can't afford to die here!

07:37.090 --> 07:39.100
Are you injured, Princess?

07:39.100 --> 07:39.800
Not really.

07:44.750 --> 07:47.540
Why would you keep something 
so important here?!

07:47.540 --> 07:48.390
You birdbrain!

07:48.390 --> 07:50.060
What's the meaning of this?

07:50.060 --> 07:51.200
It's them...

07:51.200 --> 07:52.070
It must be!

07:52.070 --> 07:53.890
They're the reason why the princess is...

07:53.890 --> 07:55.690
Capture those girls!

07:55.690 --> 07:57.790
Make sure they don't escape!

07:59.010 --> 07:59.910
Okay, let's go!

08:00.210 --> 08:01.360
Get moving!

08:01.360 --> 08:03.740
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

08:07.800 --> 08:09.540
Why'd you let them get away?!

08:09.540 --> 08:13.420
I'll tell the princess to turn 
all of you into tokoroten!

08:13.740 --> 08:15.600
Not good, not good.

08:15.600 --> 08:19.510
Looking at the button and her reaction, 
it's best to separate the two.

08:19.510 --> 08:21.220
And here I thought I was being cautious.

08:21.220 --> 08:23.010
I was a fool, damn it!

08:26.950 --> 08:28.360
You called?

08:28.610 --> 08:30.690
What kind of question is that?

08:30.690 --> 08:31.980
You big lunk.

08:31.980 --> 08:34.290
We're moving the princess 
to another location.

08:34.290 --> 08:34.830
Why?

08:34.830 --> 08:36.930
Because those girls who 
got away, thanks to <i>you</i>,

08:36.930 --> 08:38.860
might come back and steal her away!

08:38.860 --> 08:40.590
Isn't it obvious?!

08:40.900 --> 08:43.880
She may not agree to that.

08:43.880 --> 08:46.470
She's quite fond of that apartment.

08:46.470 --> 08:48.670
Who cares how fond or attached she is to it?!

08:49.090 --> 08:51.810
What, you think <i>you</i> can protect the princess?!

08:51.810 --> 08:52.810
Of course.

08:52.810 --> 08:56.710
If they touch a single hair on 
her head, you'll pay the price!

08:56.710 --> 08:57.460
Hey!

08:57.460 --> 08:58.630
Get me a hand trolley!

08:58.630 --> 09:00.010
And some security guards!

09:02.140 --> 09:05.600
You think maybe that wasn't Yoka-chan?

09:05.600 --> 09:06.450
Huh?

09:06.450 --> 09:07.680
I mean, something's up.

09:07.990 --> 09:09.860
That Yoka-chan was weird.

09:09.860 --> 09:12.680
She didn't even know who we were.

09:12.680 --> 09:15.200
Something <i>was</i> weird about her, but...

09:15.200 --> 09:17.450
I'm pretty sure that was the real Yoka.

09:18.620 --> 09:19.950
I agree.

09:19.950 --> 09:22.750
Pochi-san thought it was her, too.

09:22.750 --> 09:24.500
It's gotta be Yoka-chan.

09:24.500 --> 09:27.700
So was she just seriously angry, then?

09:27.700 --> 09:28.950
Is she ghosting us?

09:28.950 --> 09:30.160
Ghosting us?

09:30.420 --> 09:31.810
Maybe.

09:31.810 --> 09:34.810
If I was in her shoes, I probably would.

09:36.160 --> 09:37.850
Huh? What?

09:38.360 --> 09:41.380
This is Morse. Morse code!

09:41.380 --> 09:43.140
It's Zenjiro-san and Makoto-sensei!

09:43.490 --> 09:45.850
Why are they using bitter melon?

09:45.850 --> 09:49.010
The roots and vines might have grown 
to connect all the way to Agano.

09:49.400 --> 09:50.320
What?

09:50.320 --> 09:52.550
From here to Agano?

09:54.100 --> 09:55.200
Bitter melon's unstoppable!

09:55.560 --> 09:57.890
So what's Makoto-sensei saying?

09:57.890 --> 09:59.890
"Slice up a bitter melon."

09:59.890 --> 10:00.430
Huh?

10:00.430 --> 10:01.940
Shizuru-chan, knife.

10:04.860 --> 10:06.120
<i>Test, test.</i>

10:07.240 --> 10:08.130
What?

10:08.130 --> 10:10.640
The bitter melon is talking 
with Makoto-sensei's voice!

10:10.640 --> 10:12.700
Are we even speaking the 
same language anymore?

10:14.900 --> 10:17.050
<i>Not so loud! I can hear you!</i>

10:17.050 --> 10:18.660
Makoto-sensei!

10:19.960 --> 10:21.870
Hey! Can you see me?

10:21.870 --> 10:24.070
<i>No. This is a voice-only line.</i>

10:24.070 --> 10:25.010
Too bad.

10:25.010 --> 10:27.670
<i>We figured out how to turn 
the world back to normal.</i>

10:27.670 --> 10:28.900
Huh? Who's that?

10:28.900 --> 10:30.380
That's Zenjiro-san!

10:30.380 --> 10:31.660
You figured it out?

10:31.660 --> 10:35.660
<i>We haven't found proof, 
but it's a fairly credible hypothesis.</i>

10:35.930 --> 10:39.950
<i>The 7G launch should have begun 
with a switch—a button.</i>

10:39.950 --> 10:42.840
<i>And that button has been 
pressed on this whole time.</i>

10:42.840 --> 10:45.660
<i>Which means if we push it 
once more to turn it off...</i>

10:45.660 --> 10:46.370
If we push it?

10:46.720 --> 10:48.650
It should cut off the 7G network.

10:48.650 --> 10:51.340
The effects of its signal should disappear.

10:51.340 --> 10:53.930
In other words, we might 
go back to how things were.

10:54.640 --> 10:55.880
That's all?

10:55.880 --> 10:56.900
No way!

10:56.900 --> 10:58.160
That's too easy!

10:58.160 --> 10:59.870
<i>Precisely why we had overlooked it.</i>

11:00.200 --> 11:03.090
We had our hands full dealing 
with each individual phenomenon,

11:03.090 --> 11:06.160
leaving us with no time to identify 
the fundamental cause behind it all.

11:06.160 --> 11:07.790
<i>I suppose that's true.</i>

11:07.790 --> 11:09.810
<i>Where's that button, then?</i>

11:09.810 --> 11:11.110
We don't know.

11:11.110 --> 11:13.900
That said, if I were Pontaro,

11:13.900 --> 11:16.610
I'd hide it and implement 
strict security measures.

11:16.610 --> 11:19.090
In a battle between those 
preserving the new status quo

11:19.090 --> 11:21.840
and those trying to return to the old ways,

11:21.840 --> 11:24.500
the winner is decided by 
whoever has that button.

11:24.830 --> 11:27.840
<i>We'll contact you again 
once we have more information.</i>

11:27.840 --> 11:30.880
<i>Make sure you eat the bitter melon 
you used for this call.</i>

11:30.880 --> 11:31.990
Yes.

11:31.990 --> 11:34.500
<i>Don't let that food go to wast—
choo choo-choo choo...</i>

11:35.070 --> 11:37.380
Huh? He's back to the usual Zenjiro-san.

11:37.380 --> 11:42.850
<i>I've been able to extend his time in anti-
choo-choo mode to 5 minutes and 38 seconds.</i>

11:42.850 --> 11:44.120
That's incredible!

11:44.120 --> 11:47.150
<i>No, I'm still far off from 
complete anti-choo-choo.</i>

11:47.150 --> 11:49.710
<i>If you keep on extending it, 
will he go back to normal?</i>

11:49.710 --> 11:52.280
My calculations say it'll take 94 years.

11:53.880 --> 11:55.020
I see.

11:55.020 --> 11:56.980
We need to think about this.

11:56.980 --> 12:00.540
Any way you look at it, Zenjiro-san's 
not gonna be around in 94 years, is he?

12:00.540 --> 12:01.760
Not about that.

12:01.760 --> 12:03.190
You mean the button?

12:03.190 --> 12:07.470
Basically, there exists something 
along the lines of the nuclear football.

12:07.470 --> 12:08.740
Huh? What's that?

12:08.740 --> 12:11.870
A device that allows the president 
to launch nuclear weapons.

12:11.870 --> 12:13.820
His security detail carries it at all times.

12:13.820 --> 12:15.190
Isn't that risky?

12:15.190 --> 12:17.020
What if someone steals it from them?

12:17.020 --> 12:19.930
There are loads of books and 
movies about exactly that,

12:19.930 --> 12:21.700
but it's never happened in real life.

12:21.700 --> 12:22.310
Hey...

12:22.310 --> 12:26.320
Do you think that button is why 
Yoka-chan was acting so distant?

12:26.320 --> 12:27.310
What do you mean?

12:27.310 --> 12:29.900
If the world changed 
with the push of a button,

12:29.900 --> 12:31.810
then maybe if we press it again 
and turn it off,

12:31.810 --> 12:33.980
both the world and Yoka-chan 
will go back to normal.

12:33.980 --> 12:35.370
Oh, I get it now!

12:35.370 --> 12:37.690
So that's why she was being so nasty!

12:37.690 --> 12:38.760
Hold on.

12:38.760 --> 12:39.840
Is that really it?

12:39.840 --> 12:42.060
Well, that's the only explanation!

12:42.060 --> 12:43.160
How simple of you.

12:43.160 --> 12:44.350
People change.

12:44.350 --> 12:45.520
But it's worth a shot.

12:45.520 --> 12:46.890
I want to find that button.

12:48.220 --> 12:50.700
If it really is worth a shot, 
I'm going to go for it.

12:50.970 --> 12:52.690
Sounds good! I'm all for it!

12:52.690 --> 12:53.440
What if...

12:53.440 --> 12:55.630
There goes Akira with 
her ifs, ands, or buts!

12:55.630 --> 12:56.510
Hear me out!

12:56.510 --> 12:59.920
It's all well and good to try and find 
the button, but where do we even look?

12:59.920 --> 13:03.080
We have two missions here: 
locating it, and taking it for ourselves.

13:08.640 --> 13:09.730
Huh?

13:09.730 --> 13:11.220
The zombies?

13:13.560 --> 13:14.980
It's Kurokin!

13:15.350 --> 13:16.650
But how?

13:17.180 --> 13:18.660
It's been a while.

13:19.770 --> 13:23.480
After you left, the climate changed 
drastically near Hoya Station.

13:23.480 --> 13:26.960
If left there, the zombies 
would have grown rotten and moldy

13:26.960 --> 13:29.060
or dried up and crumbled away.

13:29.060 --> 13:31.030
Zombies are pretty dainty, huh?

13:31.030 --> 13:31.750
Who knew?

13:31.750 --> 13:34.000
And so you want to team up with us?

13:34.480 --> 13:36.780
Our power comes from our numbers.

13:36.780 --> 13:39.510
And you have brains? I guess?

13:39.510 --> 13:40.620
Why do you sound so unsure?

13:40.620 --> 13:43.600
We just heard from Makoto-sensei, 
the brains on our team,

13:43.600 --> 13:47.770
and the answer to our problems may lie 
in finding the button to stop 7G.

13:47.770 --> 13:49.570
The brains on our team? Huh?

13:49.570 --> 13:51.440
That makes you the dumb muscle.

13:51.440 --> 13:53.280
Where do we find that button?

13:53.280 --> 13:54.360
We don't know.

13:54.360 --> 13:57.810
But it's powerful enough to have turned 
the entire world into what it is now.

13:57.810 --> 13:59.520
So it should be pretty big.

13:59.520 --> 14:01.740
Oh, like a sake barrel?

14:01.740 --> 14:03.090
A sake barrel?

14:03.090 --> 14:03.940
What's up?

14:03.940 --> 14:04.680
Well...

14:04.680 --> 14:07.220
When we were passing by 
the department store...

14:09.970 --> 14:11.980
Huh? What's wrong?!

14:18.980 --> 14:22.620
The zombies showed interest in something 
other than brains and cauliflower.

14:22.940 --> 14:25.500
Zombies want to go back to being human.

14:25.500 --> 14:31.460
Perhaps they were reacting to the 
button that has that potential.

14:31.890 --> 14:34.650
There's a good chance that 
what I saw was that button.

14:34.650 --> 14:36.880
Huh... But there's also a chance it wasn't.

14:36.880 --> 14:38.440
That department store, huh?

14:38.440 --> 14:39.830
I've never been.

14:39.830 --> 14:40.490
Huh?

14:40.490 --> 14:42.210
What was it? "Life should be trendy"?

14:42.210 --> 14:43.880
And "Fall in love with yourself"?

14:43.880 --> 14:46.730
I've wanted to go ever since I saw 
those ad slogans a long time ago.

14:46.730 --> 14:47.880
What, you're dying to go?

14:47.880 --> 14:49.980
We came all this way to Ikebukuro!

14:49.980 --> 14:51.350
What's wrong with taking a look?

14:51.350 --> 14:53.370
You just want to check out 
the department store!

14:53.370 --> 14:54.630
To go shopping!

14:54.630 --> 14:56.270
Just on the side!

14:56.270 --> 14:57.820
I'll look for that button, too!

14:57.820 --> 14:58.490
You big, fat liar!

14:58.490 --> 15:01.150
I wouldn't put it past Pontaro to hide it.

15:01.150 --> 15:02.820
He was acting real high-and-mighty.

15:03.080 --> 15:04.890
Poison Pontaro?

15:04.890 --> 15:06.980
I've heard nothing but 
sketchy rumors about him.

15:06.980 --> 15:09.940
Zenjiro-san called him a poopy dunghead, too.

15:09.940 --> 15:12.060
Said he thinks about nothing but himself.

15:12.640 --> 15:15.560
He's involved with 7G, isn't he?

15:15.560 --> 15:18.450
But he's not trying to fix it. 
He's lording over everyone instead.

15:18.450 --> 15:22.350
Well, who'd want to be held responsible 
for creating this huge mess?

15:22.350 --> 15:25.150
How awful can you be, not taking 
responsibility for what you did?!

15:26.120 --> 15:28.820
I see, like a zombie. In a bad sense.

15:28.820 --> 15:29.400
What?

15:29.400 --> 15:32.960
Short-sighted, only worried 
about yourself in the present.

15:32.960 --> 15:34.490
No remorse, no thinking ahead.

15:34.940 --> 15:36.220
What's wrong?

15:36.220 --> 15:39.120
It's not... entirely nothing.

15:39.120 --> 15:40.860
Should we go to the department store?

15:40.860 --> 15:41.740
I'm down!

15:41.740 --> 15:43.590
What about Yoka-chan?

15:43.590 --> 15:44.920
Maybe she's a lost cause...

15:44.920 --> 15:45.690
What?!

15:45.690 --> 15:47.010
A lost cause how?!

15:47.010 --> 15:48.440
She <i>did</i> ghost us...

15:48.440 --> 15:50.070
There you go again!

15:50.070 --> 15:51.560
Listen, Shizuru-chan.

15:51.560 --> 15:53.950
Now's really not the time for this.

15:53.950 --> 15:55.430
You're scaring me, Nadeko-chan.

15:55.430 --> 15:57.380
I want to go see Yoka-chan.

15:57.380 --> 15:59.190
Even if you don't, I will!

15:59.190 --> 16:00.790
I want to see her, too!

16:00.790 --> 16:02.140
Weren't you going shopping?

16:02.140 --> 16:02.980
Nuh-uh!

16:02.980 --> 16:04.230
Are you listening, Shizuru-chan?

16:04.230 --> 16:05.980
Does it matter if I am?

16:05.980 --> 16:08.200
You're going to talk to her, 
whether you want to or not.

16:08.200 --> 16:08.850
What?!

16:09.650 --> 16:10.560
What?!

16:19.460 --> 16:21.880
We'll have to search every nook 
and cranny of this place!

16:21.880 --> 16:23.080
Why do you sound so smug?

16:23.080 --> 16:26.440
I never thought I'd get to say 
"search every nook and cranny" in real life.

16:26.440 --> 16:27.130
Ah.

16:27.130 --> 16:28.360
Like, "You homewrecker!"

16:28.360 --> 16:30.500
Or, "Consider it a parting gift."

16:30.500 --> 16:33.350
I've always wanted to say, 
"What are you, blind?"

16:33.350 --> 16:35.370
That's what I'm talking about, Kurokin!

16:35.370 --> 16:38.320
There's plenty of phrases you 
never get a chance to say.

16:38.320 --> 16:40.440
Phrases you didn't get a chance to say...

16:41.510 --> 16:43.730
You need to tell her, Shizuru-chan.

16:44.810 --> 16:45.650
Yeah.

16:53.110 --> 16:53.880
What?

16:53.880 --> 16:55.370
Maybe they found it!

17:00.110 --> 17:01.950
Put these away! Hurry!

17:02.210 --> 17:04.200
Can I help you find something?

17:04.200 --> 17:06.020
That's one of our top sellers.

17:06.020 --> 17:07.130
It'd look great on you.

17:07.130 --> 17:08.930
Ugh, I can't stand it!

17:08.930 --> 17:10.570
That insistent smile!

17:10.940 --> 17:11.790
There's so many!

17:11.790 --> 17:14.800
They'll chase you down if you run. There's only one way out of this!

17:15.380 --> 17:16.970
I'm just looking!

17:21.220 --> 17:23.680
World-renowned artists!

17:22.770 --> 17:24.430
Pay in easy installments!

17:23.680 --> 17:25.910
Painted by a living treasure...

17:24.860 --> 17:26.930
A once-in-a-lifetime chance!

17:26.930 --> 17:27.650
Outta my way!

17:27.650 --> 17:29.700
You can pay for the damage, right?

17:29.700 --> 17:32.560
No way in hell we're paying!

17:32.930 --> 17:35.600
Don't try to sucker us into forking over our cash!

17:37.450 --> 17:39.350
The zombies are reacting to something!

17:39.350 --> 17:40.290
Is it the button?!

17:40.290 --> 17:41.380
What was that?!

17:41.380 --> 17:43.660
A suspicious group in the department store?

17:43.660 --> 17:46.290
The vigilance committee 
is headed there as we speak.

17:46.290 --> 17:48.420
They're really after the button, huh?

17:48.420 --> 17:50.690
Wait, how'd they know where it was?

17:51.500 --> 17:53.750
Do we have a traitor?

17:53.750 --> 17:55.890
By which I mean, an intelligence leak?

17:55.890 --> 17:57.250
That's unthinkable!

17:57.690 --> 17:59.300
How about this, then?

18:01.720 --> 18:03.180
You understand, don't you?

18:03.490 --> 18:05.120
What's your job?

18:05.120 --> 18:07.640
To protect Yoka-sama.

18:09.300 --> 18:11.680
In which case, do away with those brats

18:11.680 --> 18:13.940
and dump their bodies 
all the way out past Zoshigaya!

18:13.940 --> 18:15.650
And protect that button!

18:15.650 --> 18:18.360
If they get ahold of that button, 
this world won't stay the same!

18:18.360 --> 18:21.590
The masses will start violent riots 
and lose all control.

18:21.590 --> 18:25.580
If that happens, your precious 
little Yoka-sama won't be safe.

18:26.170 --> 18:29.520
Protecting the princess and the 
button are essentially the same!

18:29.520 --> 18:30.620
They're equal!

18:30.620 --> 18:32.970
Don't let it fall into their hands!

18:43.800 --> 18:45.360
There's something in the pond!

18:45.360 --> 18:46.240
The button!

18:46.240 --> 18:48.180
Why are they reacting to the button?

18:48.180 --> 18:50.720
They're a product of the changes caused by 7G.

18:50.720 --> 18:54.450
Maybe they're responding to its energy 
or longing for the world we used to live in.

18:54.450 --> 18:55.770
Either way, they can sense it.

18:56.100 --> 18:58.210
We just need to push the button, right?

18:58.210 --> 18:59.240
Yeah.

18:59.540 --> 19:00.270
There they are!

19:00.270 --> 19:01.160
Not again!

19:01.160 --> 19:02.860
I'll take care of these guys,

19:02.860 --> 19:04.430
so you go get that button!

19:03.760 --> 19:04.740
I'll help you out!

19:04.740 --> 19:06.010
Our job is to grab the button!

19:14.120 --> 19:16.950
Zombies can't go in water! 
They'll get waterlogged!

19:25.140 --> 19:26.010
Who are you?

19:26.010 --> 19:27.340
My name is Pochi.

19:27.630 --> 19:28.630
Pochi?

19:29.120 --> 19:29.990
You're not Pochi...

19:34.750 --> 19:35.450
How?!

19:35.450 --> 19:37.110
I feel the same way.

19:37.110 --> 19:38.050
What?!

19:38.050 --> 19:39.400
I'll protect Yoka-sama.

19:52.010 --> 19:53.330
Does Yoka...

19:53.330 --> 19:56.080
Does Yoka like things the way they are now?!

19:56.080 --> 19:58.350
She devotes herself to studying every day.

19:58.350 --> 19:59.350
Still!

19:59.670 --> 20:01.670
People call her a witch and stuff!

20:01.670 --> 20:04.750
That is not something Yoka-sama 
has to answer for.

20:10.980 --> 20:13.480
It doesn't matter what anyone says about her.

20:13.480 --> 20:16.320
Yoka-sama is perfectly fine the way she is.

20:24.290 --> 20:26.250
Reimi-chan! Shizuru-chan!

20:29.880 --> 20:31.970
We got the button!

20:31.970 --> 20:32.990
Press it!

20:32.990 --> 20:34.600
Hurry!

20:48.020 --> 20:50.510
Did 7G stop?

20:57.770 --> 20:58.840
It's no use!

20:58.840 --> 20:59.570
But why?!

21:00.140 --> 21:01.520
No way!

21:04.000 --> 21:06.090
Zombie 35! 72!

21:06.090 --> 21:06.970
Get away!

21:06.970 --> 21:08.650
You're in danger!

21:11.400 --> 21:12.710
Shizuru-chan!

21:13.720 --> 21:14.830
Don't, Pochi-san!

21:16.170 --> 21:17.360
Pochi-san...

21:17.900 --> 21:20.080
I can't fight you.

21:45.330 --> 21:46.080
What?

21:50.560 --> 21:51.850
Yoka-chan!

21:52.790 --> 21:54.210
She's on board!

21:55.060 --> 21:56.560
You damn fools.

21:56.560 --> 21:58.160
Ikebukuro is safe and sound.

21:59.020 --> 22:00.670
As long as it has its princess, that is.
